---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/ias/ias1.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope & Definitions" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Overall Considerations" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Complete Set of Statements" },
        { id: "s5", label: "SoFP – Structure" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Illustrative SoFP" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Current/Non-Current" },
        { id: "s8", label: "SoPL & OCI – Structure" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Illustrative SoPL – By Function" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Illustrative SoPL – By Nature" },
        { id: "s11", label: "OCI – Two Groups" },
        { id: "s12", label: "SoCE – Structure" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Illustrative SoCE" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Cash Flow Statement" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Notes & Policies" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Judgements & Estimates" },
        { id: "s17", label: "IFRS vs US GAAP" },
        { id: "s18", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s19", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s20", label: "Glossary" },
        { id: "history", label: "History & Development" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span
        class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Why presentation is a Framework issue</div>
        <div class="principle">
          The Conceptual Framework states that the objective of general purpose
          financial statements is to provide information useful to users in
          making decisions about providing resources to the entity. IAS 1
          operationalises HOW that information is structured so it is
          understandable and comparable. It does not itself prescribe
          recognition or measurement – those sit in the substantive standards.
        </div>
        <div class="elabel">IAS 1 AND THE QUALITATIVE CHARACTERISTICS</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span
            ><strong>Comparability</strong> – consistent structure and classification
            from period to period; comparative information for the prior period</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Understandability</strong> – clear titles; aggregation of similar
            items; separate presentation of dissimilar items when material</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Faithful representation</strong> – fair presentation achieved
            through compliance with IFRS; in extremely rare cases a departure where
            compliance would be misleading (the "true and fair override")</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cs">
        <div class="ctitle cs">
          Measurement vs presentation – the key distinction
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          IAS 1 is almost entirely a PRESENTATION standard. It prescribes WHERE
          assets, liabilities, equity, income and expenses appear and how they
          are grouped – not how individual items are measured (those rules sit
          in other standards such as IFRS 9, IAS 16, IFRS 15).
        </div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;">
            <span>Framework concept</span><span>IAS 1 role</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;">
            <span>Elements (assets; liabilities; equity; income; expenses)</span
            ><span
              >Prescribes WHERE each element appears and how groups are
              organised</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;">
            <span>Going concern</span><span
              >A fundamental assumption management must explicitly assess;
              uncertainties disclosed</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr;">
            <span>Materiality</span><span
              >Drives aggregation, disaggregation, and disclosure decisions
              throughout IAS 1</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout info" style="margin-bottom:0;">
          IAS 1 does not prescribe a rigid single-format template – it sets
          minimum line items and overarching principles, leaving significant
          structural flexibility to preparers.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S2 – SCOPE & DEFINITIONS ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope &amp; Key Definitions</h2><span
        class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">What IAS 1 covers – and what it does not</div>
        <div class="principle">
          IAS 1 sets out the overall requirements for the presentation of
          general purpose financial statements, guidelines for their structure,
          and minimum requirements for their content – to ensure comparability
          both with the entity's own prior periods and with other entities
          applying IFRS.
        </div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span
            >All general purpose financial statements prepared under IFRS for
            profit-oriented entities</span
          >
          <span>Consolidated financial statements of a group</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cross-list" style="margin-top:6px;">
          <span
            >Condensed interim financial statements → <strong>IAS 34</strong
            ></span
          >
          <span
            >Recognition, measurement, disclosure of specific transactions →
            relevant substantive standard (IFRS 15; IAS 16 etc.)</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          IAS 1 does not mandate the titles "statement of financial position" or
          "statement of profit or loss" – entities may retain traditional names
          ("balance sheet"; "income statement") as long as they are not
          misleading.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Key definitions</div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">General purpose financial statements</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Financial statements intended to meet the needs of users who are not
            in a position to require an entity to prepare reports tailored to
            their particular information needs.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Impracticable</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Applying a requirement is impracticable when the entity cannot apply
            it after making every reasonable effort to do so. A key threshold
            used when considering whether to restate comparative information.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Material</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Information is material if omitting, misstating, or obscuring it
            could reasonably be expected to influence decisions of the primary
            users of those financial statements.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Other comprehensive income (OCI)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Items of income and expense that are not recognised in profit or
            loss as required or permitted by other IFRS Standards – presented in
            a separate section of the statement(s) of profit or loss and OCI.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S3 – OVERALL CONSIDERATIONS ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span><h2>
        Overall Considerations – The Core Principles
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">
          Eight overarching principles that pervade every IAS 1 requirement
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span
                ><strong>Fair presentation:</strong> financial statements shall present
                fairly the financial position, financial performance, and cash flows
                of an entity. Fair presentation requires the faithful representation
                of the effects of transactions, other events and conditions in accordance
                with the definitions and recognition criteria for assets, liabilities,
                income and expenses set out in the Conceptual Framework.</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Compliance with IFRS:</strong> an entity whose financial
                statements comply with IFRS Standards shall make an explicit and unreserved
                statement of such compliance in the notes. An entity shall not describe
                financial statements as complying with IFRS unless they comply with
                all the requirements.</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Going concern:</strong> management shall make an assessment
                of an entity's ability to continue as a going concern. When material
                uncertainties exist, they must be disclosed; if the going concern
                basis is not used, IAS 1 requires this fact to be disclosed together
                with the basis on which the financial statements have been prepared.</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Accrual basis:</strong> an entity shall prepare its financial
                statements using the accrual basis of accounting, except for cash
                flow information – the only primary statement on a cash basis (IAS
                7).</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span
                ><strong>Materiality and aggregation:</strong> each material class
                of similar items shall be presented separately; items of a dissimilar
                nature or function shall be presented separately unless they are immaterial.
                Aggregation of immaterial items is acceptable and may improve clarity.</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>No offsetting:</strong> assets and liabilities, and income
                and expenses, shall not be offset unless required or permitted by
                an IFRS Standard. Offsetting obscures both the gross amounts and the
                nature of individual items.</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Frequency of reporting:</strong> an entity shall present
                a complete set of financial statements at least annually. When the
                end of the reporting period changes and annual statements are presented
                for longer or shorter than one year, additional disclosures are required.</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Comparative information:</strong> unless an IFRS Standard
                permits or requires otherwise, an entity shall present comparative
                information in respect of the prior period for all amounts reported
                in the current period's financial statements. A third SoFP is required
                when an entity applies an accounting policy retrospectively or makes
                a retrospective restatement or reclassification that materially affects
                the prior period SoFP (IAS 8).</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S4 – COMPLETE SET ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span><h2>
        A Complete Set of Financial Statements
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">
          Six required components and the comparative period rules
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="check-list">
              <span
                ><strong>Statement of financial position (SoFP)</strong> as at the
                end of the period – 2 years minimum (3 if restated)</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong
                  >Statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income
                  (SoPL&amp;OCI)</strong
                > for the period – 2 years</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Statement of changes in equity (SoCE)</strong> for the period
                – 2 years</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Statement of cash flows (SCF)</strong> for the period – 2
                years (governed in detail by IAS 7)</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Notes</strong> comprising significant accounting policies
                and other explanatory information</span
              >
              <span
                ><strong>Comparative information</strong> – prior period for all amounts;
                prior period notes where relevant</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="callout warn" style="margin-bottom:8px;">
              <strong>Third balance sheet (SoFP):</strong> required as at the beginning
              of the earliest comparative period when an entity (a) applies an accounting
              policy retrospectively; (b) makes a retrospective restatement; or (c)
              reclassifies items in its financial statements – and that change has
              a material effect on the prior period SoFP. This third SoFP requires
              only the primary statement; the related notes need not be presented.
            </div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span
                >All components are of equal prominence – no single statement is
                the "primary" one</span
              >
              <span
                >Titles used are not mandated – entities retain flexibility on
                naming</span
              >
              <span
                >Minimum of 12-monthly reporting; when the period is shorter or
                longer than 12 months, disclose the reason and note comparatives
                may not be entirely comparable</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S5 – SoFP STRUCTURE ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span><h2>
        Statement of Financial Position – Structure
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Minimum line items and presentation choices</div>
        <div class="elabel">MINIMUM LINE ITEMS ON THE FACE OF THE SoFP</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span
            >Property, plant and equipment; investment property; intangible
            assets; financial assets; equity-accounted investments</span
          >
          <span
            >Biological assets; inventories; trade and other receivables</span
          >
          <span>Cash and cash equivalents; assets held for sale (IFRS 5)</span>
          <span
            >Trade and other payables; provisions; financial liabilities</span
          >
          <span
            >Current and deferred tax assets/liabilities; liabilities in
            disposal groups (IFRS 5)</span
          >
          <span
            >Non-controlling interests within equity; issued capital and
            reserves</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          Additional line items, headings and subtotals are added whenever
          relevant to understanding the entity's financial position. An entity
          uses its judgement about whether to present further
          sub-classifications on the face or in the notes.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">
          Presentation approach – two permitted formats
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div class="spec-box">
            <div class="spec-title">Current / non-current distinction</div>
            <div class="spec-desc">
              Separate current and non-current assets, and current and
              non-current liabilities, as distinct classifications. The most
              common format for industrial and commercial entities. Uses the IAS
              1 current/non-current criteria.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-box" style="margin-bottom:0;">
            <div class="spec-title">Order of liquidity</div>
            <div class="spec-desc">
              Items presented broadly in order of liquidity – no
              current/non-current split. Used when this provides more relevant
              information (e.g. banks; financial institutions where assets and
              liabilities are managed on a liquidity basis).
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout info" style="margin-bottom:0;">
          A mixed approach is permitted: current/non-current for some assets and
          liabilities, and order of liquidity for others – when this provides
          more relevant information (e.g. an entity that has both financial and
          non-financial operations).
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S6 – ILLUSTRATIVE SoFP ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span><h2>
        Illustrative Statement of Financial Position
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">
          Statement of Financial Position – blank format then illustrative
          example
        </div>
        <div class="fmt-label">
          FORMAT – X = positive amount &nbsp;·&nbsp; (X) = negative / deduction
          &nbsp;·&nbsp; – = nil
        </div>
        <div class="fs-wrap fmt">
          <div class="fs-head">
            <div class="fs-entity">Entity Name</div>
            <div class="fs-title">Statement of Financial Position</div>
            <div class="fs-date">As at [reporting date]</div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-cols"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span></span><span style="text-align:center;">Note</span><span
              style="text-align:center;">Current yr</span
            ><span style="text-align:center;">Prior yr</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fs-section">ASSETS</div>
          <div class="fs-subsection">Non-current assets</div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Property, plant and equipment</span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Right-of-use assets</span><span class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Intangible assets</span><span class="num-right">X</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Investments in associates (equity method)</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>FVOCI financial assets</span><span class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Deferred tax assets</span><span class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row subtotal"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Total non-current assets</span><span></span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fs-subsection">Current assets</div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Inventories</span><span class="num-right">X</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Trade and other receivables</span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Contract assets (IFRS 15)</span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Current tax receivable</span><span class="num-right">–</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Cash and cash equivalents</span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row subtotal"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Total current assets</span><span></span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row doubletotal"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>TOTAL ASSETS</span><span></span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fs-section">EQUITY AND LIABILITIES</div>
          <div class="fs-subsection">
            Equity attributable to owners of the parent
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Share capital</span><span class="num-right">X</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Share premium</span><span class="num-right">–</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Retained earnings</span><span class="num-right">–</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Revaluation reserve</span><span class="num-right">–</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>FVOCI reserve [may be (X) if net loss position]</span><span
              class="num-right">–</span
            ><span class="num-right">X/(X)</span><span class="num-right"
              >X/(X)</span
            >
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row subtotal"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Total – attributable to owners of parent</span><span
            ></span><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            >
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Non-controlling interests</span><span class="num-right"
              >–</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row subtotal"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Total equity</span><span></span><span class="num-right"
              >X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fs-subsection">Non-current liabilities</div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Bank borrowings</span><span class="num-right">X</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Lease liabilities</span><span class="num-right">X</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Deferred tax liabilities</span><span class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row alt indent1"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
          >
            <span>Post-employment benefit obligations</span><span
              class="num-right">X</span
            ><span class="num-right">X</span><span class="num-right">X</span>
          </div>
          <div
            class="fs-row subtotal"
            style="grid-template-columns:2.2fr 0.3fr 0.6fr 0.6fr;"
