    <!-- ═══ S11 – OCI TWO GROUPS ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span><h2>
        OCI – Two Groups and the Recycling Rule
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">
          IAS 1 mandates that OCI items are grouped by whether they will or will
          not be reclassified to profit or loss
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">
              GROUP 1 – WILL NOT BE RECLASSIFIED ("NEVER RECYCLED")
            </div>
            <div class="td-table">
              <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span>OCI item</span><span>Standard</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span>Revaluation surplus on PP&amp;E or intangibles</span><span
                  >IAS 16/IAS 38</span
                >
              </div>
              <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >Remeasurements of defined benefit plan (actuarial
                  gains/losses)</span
                ><span>IAS 19</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >FVOCI equity investments – changes in fair value (irrevocable
                  election)</span
                ><span>IFRS 9</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >Own credit risk on financial liabilities designated at FVTPL</span
                ><span>IFRS 9</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="note">
              Items in Group 1 are permanently in equity. A revaluation surplus
              may be transferred directly to retained earnings (depreciation or
              disposal) but it is never reclassified through profit or loss.
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">
              GROUP 2 – MAY BE RECLASSIFIED ("RECYCLABLE")
            </div>
            <div class="td-table">
              <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span>OCI item</span><span>Standard</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >Exchange differences on translating foreign operations</span
                ><span>IAS 21</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >Cash flow hedge – effective portion of gains/losses on
                  hedging instrument</span
                ><span>IFRS 9</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >FVOCI debt instruments – cumulative fair value changes</span
                ><span>IFRS 9</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span>Net investment hedge – effective portion (IAS 21)</span
                ><span>IFRS 9/IAS 21</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.8fr 0.8fr;">
                <span
                  >Share of OCI of associates/joint ventures (recyclable items)</span
                ><span>IAS 28</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="note">
              Group 2 items accumulate in OCI (equity) and are "recycled"
              (reclassified) to profit or loss in a future period when the
              related item is derecognised, sold, or the hedged transaction
              affects profit or loss.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S12 – SoCE STRUCTURE ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span><h2>
        Statement of Changes in Equity – Structure
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">
          What IAS 1 requires the SoCE to show – five mandatory elements
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="check-list">
              <span
                >Total comprehensive income for the period – split between
                amounts attributable to owners of the parent and to
                non-controlling interests</span
              >
              <span
                >For each component of equity, the effects of retrospective
                application or restatement recognised in accordance with IAS 8</span
              >
              <span
                >For each component of equity, a reconciliation between the
                opening and closing carrying amount, disclosing separately: (a)
                profit or loss; (b) each item of OCI; (c) transactions with
                owners (contributions; distributions; changes in ownership
                without loss of control)</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="check-list">
              <span
                >Amount of dividends recognised as distributions to owners (and
                dividends per share) – either on the face or in the notes</span
              >
              <span
                >For each component – a column per component is the most common
                presentation (share capital; share premium; retained earnings;
                each OCI reserve; NCI; total)</span
              >
            </div>
            <div class="callout warn" style="margin-top:6px;margin-bottom:0;">
              <strong>IAS 8 restatements:</strong> prior period errors and voluntary
              retrospective policy changes are shown as adjustments to opening retained
              earnings – NOT as items flowing through profit or loss in the current
              year. The corrected opening balance is the starting point; a third SoFP
              may be needed.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

