    <!-- ═══ S14 – CASH FLOW ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s14">
      <span class="num">14</span><h2>
        Statement of Cash Flows – Overview (IAS 7)
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd">
        <div class="ctitle cd">
          The one primary statement not governed by IAS 1 – IAS 7 provides the
          detailed rules
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          IAS 1 requires a statement of cash flows to be presented as part of a
          complete set of financial statements, but delegates all its detailed
          requirements to IAS 7. It is the only primary statement prepared on a
          cash basis rather than the accrual basis.
        </div>
        <div class="elabel">THREE SECTIONS – ALL STATEMENTS MUST SHOW</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;">
            <span>Section</span><span>Content</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;">
            <span><strong>Operating</strong></span><span
              >Cash generated from the entity's principal revenue-producing
              activities. May use direct method (gross cash receipts and
              payments) or indirect method (profit adjusted for non-cash items
              and working capital changes). Indirect method is by far the more
              common in practice.</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;">
            <span><strong>Investing</strong></span><span
              >Cash flows from acquisition and disposal of long-term assets and
              investments not classified as cash equivalents. Always presented
              gross (direct method) – e.g. proceeds from sale of PP&E; payments
              to acquire subsidiaries.</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;">
            <span><strong>Financing</strong></span><span
              >Cash flows that result in changes in the size and composition of
              equity and borrowings – proceeds from share issues; repayment of
              borrowings; dividends paid; lease repayments (IFRS 16). Always
              presented gross.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Key IAS 7 classification choices and traps</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span
            ><strong>Interest paid:</strong> may be classified as operating (most
            common – matching the P&L finance cost) or financing (it represents borrowing
            costs). Policy choice; applied consistently.</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Interest received:</strong> may be operating (return on investments)
            or investing. Policy choice.</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Dividends paid:</strong> may be financing (most common – distributions
            to owners) or operating. Policy choice.</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Dividends received:</strong> may be operating or investing. Policy
            choice.</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Taxes:</strong> generally operating unless specifically identifiable
            with financing or investing.</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Lease payments (IFRS 16):</strong> principal portion of lease
            liability repayments → financing; interest portion → operating or financing
            (policy choice); short-term and low-value lease payments → operating.</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="callout warn" style="margin-bottom:0;margin-top:6px;">
          The indirect method reconciles profit/loss to cash from operations.
          Key adjustments: <strong>add back</strong> depreciation/amortisation (non-cash);
          <strong>add back</strong> finance costs charged (reclassified to financing);
          <strong>deduct</strong> investment income (reclassified to investing); <strong
            >adjust</strong
          > for working capital changes (inventory; receivables; payables).
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S15 – NOTES & POLICIES ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s15">
      <span class="num">15</span><h2>Notes &amp; Accounting Policies</h2><span
        class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Structure and purpose of notes</div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span
            >Present information about the basis of preparation and the specific
            accounting policies used</span
          >
          <span
            >Disclose information required by IFRS Standards that is not
            presented elsewhere in the primary statements</span
          >
          <span
            >Provide information relevant to understanding the primary
            statements that is not presented on their face</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="elabel" style="margin-top:8px;">
          RECOMMENDED NOTE ORDER (IAS 1 – NOT MANDATORY)
        </div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span>Statement of compliance with IFRS and basis of preparation</span
          >
          <span>Summary of material accounting policies</span>
          <span
            >Supporting information for items presented on the face (in the same
            order as the statements)</span
          >
          <span
            >Other disclosures: contingent liabilities; unrecognised contractual
            commitments; non-financial disclosures</span
          >
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          IAS 1 no longer mandates a single fixed note ordering – entities may
          present notes in whatever order best communicates their financial
          statements to users.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cw">
        <div class="ctitle cw">
          Material accounting policy information (2023 amendment)
        </div>
        <div class="principle">
          Following the 2023 amendment, IAS 1 requires disclosure of "material
          accounting policy information" rather than a summary of all
          significant accounting policies. An accounting policy is material if
          it is expected to significantly affect the amounts or disclosures in
          the financial statements.
        </div>
        <div class="dot-list">
          <span
            ><strong>What makes a policy material:</strong> (a) an IFRS Standard allows
            a policy choice and the entity has chosen a less common option; (b) management
            has significant judgement in applying the policy; (c) the policy relates
            to a complex or unusual transaction type that is significant to the entity</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Not material:</strong> boilerplate accounting policy descriptions
            that copy IFRS wording and do not add entity-specific information do not
            meet the threshold and should be omitted to improve clarity</span
          >
          <span
            ><strong>Practical effect:</strong> entities should remove "clutter" from
            the notes – generic policy descriptions that provide no entity-specific
            insight reduce the readability and usefulness of financial statements</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S16 – JUDGEMENTS & ESTIMATES ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s16">
      <span class="num">16</span><h2>
        Critical Judgements &amp; Estimates Disclosures
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">
          Two distinct mandatory disclosures – commonly confused in practice and
          in exams
        </div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="spec-box">
              <div class="spec-title">Significant judgements (IAS 1.122)</div>
              <div class="spec-desc">
                Judgements that management has made in the process of applying
                the entity's accounting policies and that have the most
                significant effect on the amounts recognised in the financial
                statements. Focus: the decision made (not the estimate of an
                uncertain future outcome).
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span
                >Whether the entity is the principal or agent in a contract
                (IFRS 15)</span
              >
              <span>Whether a lease term includes option periods (IFRS 16)</span
              >
              <span>Whether an entity controls an investee (IFRS 10)</span>
              <span
                >Classification of a financial instrument as equity or liability
                (IAS 32)</span
              >
              <span>Whether going concern basis remains appropriate</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="spec-box">
              <div class="spec-title">
                Key sources of estimation uncertainty (IAS 1.125)
              </div>
              <div class="spec-desc">
                Key assumptions about the future, and other major sources of
                estimation uncertainty at the end of the reporting period, that
                have a significant risk of resulting in a material adjustment to
                the carrying amounts of assets and liabilities within the NEXT
                financial year.
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span
                >Expected credit loss assumptions (IFRS 9 – PD; LGD; EAD)</span
              >
              <span
                >Useful lives and residual values of property, plant and
                equipment</span
              >
              <span
                >Actuarial assumptions for defined benefit plan obligations (IAS
                19)</span
              >
              <span>Fair value measurements (Level 3 inputs) – IFRS 13</span>
              <span
                >Recoverability of deferred tax assets – judgment on future
                taxable profit</span
              >
            </div>
            <div class="callout danger" style="margin-bottom:0;margin-top:6px;">
              <strong>Key distinction:</strong> the estimation uncertainty disclosure
              has a specific <strong>12-month time horizon</strong> ("within the next
              financial year"). Uncertainties with a longer horizon are not captured
              here. The judgements disclosure has no such time horizon – it covers
              all material judgements in the current period's policies.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S17 – IFRS vs US GAAP ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s17">
      <span class="num">17</span><h2>
        IFRS vs US GAAP – Key Presentation Differences
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Feature</span><span>IFRS (IAS 1)</span><span>US GAAP</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>SoFP order</span><span
              >Free choice: liquidity order or current/non-current, whichever
              more relevant</span
            ><span
              >Typically decreasing liquidity (current assets first) for US
              public companies</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Extraordinary items</span><span
              >Prohibited – no separate classification</span
            ><span
              >Also prohibited since ASU 2015-01; infrequent/unusual items may
              be separately presented</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>OCI – presentation</span><span
              >Single or two-statement approach both permitted</span
            ><span
              >Single or two-statement approach also permitted (largely
              converged)</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Expense classification</span><span
              >Free choice: by nature or by function</span
            ><span
              >SEC registrants generally present by function (cost of revenues
              required)</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Comparative SoFP periods</span><span
              >Two years minimum (three if restated)</span
            ><span
              >Two years for most entities (three for the income statement and
              cash flows under SEC rules for large accelerated filers)</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>NCI presentation</span><span
              >Within equity – clearly labelled; never between liabilities and
              equity</span
            ><span>Within equity – same as IFRS; converged</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Offsetting rule</span><span
              >No offsetting unless required or permitted by IFRS</span
            ><span
              >Same general principle; specific guidance in ASC 210-20 on
              netting financial instruments</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.4fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Third balance sheet</span><span
              >Required on material retrospective restatements (IAS 8)</span
            ><span
              >No explicit equivalent requirement; restated comparatives
              presented but no mandated third SoFP</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          Despite convergence efforts, the SEC's stricter comparative-period
          requirements for the income statement and cash flow statement (three
          years for large accelerated filers) and the typical format differences
          in the SoFP remain practical differences for multinational preparers.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S18 – STATEMENT MAPPING ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s18">
      <span class="num">18</span><h2>
        Statement Mapping – Where Every IAS 1 Concept Lands
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>IAS 1 concept / requirement</span><span>Statement(s)</span
            ><span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Current/non-current or liquidity classification</span><span
              ><span class="badge bs">SoFP</span></span
            ><span>Structural choice; applied consistently</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>By function / by nature expense presentation</span><span
              ><span class="badge bp">SoPL</span></span
            ><span>Policy choice; function requires by-nature notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span
              >OCI – never recycled (revaluations; remeasurements; FVOCI equity)</span
            ><span><span class="badge bo">OCI</span></span><span
              >Permanently in equity; may transfer within equity</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>OCI – may recycle (FX translation; CFH; FVOCI debt)</span
            ><span
              ><span class="badge bo">OCI</span> → <span class="badge bp"
                >SoPL</span
              ></span
            ><span>Recycled on disposal/derecognition/hedged item</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Dividends declared</span><span
              ><span class="badge be">SoCE</span></span
            ><span>Distribution to owners; not an expense in SoPL</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Prior period error / retrospective policy change</span><span
              ><span class="badge be">SoCE</span>
              <span class="badge bs">SoFP</span></span
            ><span
              >Opening retained earnings restated; may trigger third SoFP (IAS
              8)</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Cash from operations; investing; financing</span><span
              ><span class="badge bc">SCF</span></span
            ><span>The only primary statement on cash basis (IAS 7)</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Significant judgements</span><span
              ><span class="badge bp">Notes</span></span
            ><span>Current period; most significant effect on amounts</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Estimation uncertainty (12-month horizon)</span><span
              ><span class="badge bp">Notes</span></span
            ><span>Risk of material adjustment within NEXT financial year</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Material accounting policy information</span><span
              ><span class="badge bp">Notes</span></span
            ><span
              >Post-2023 amendment: material policies only; not boilerplate</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>Going concern material uncertainty</span><span
              ><span class="badge bp">Notes</span></span
            ><span
              >Disclosed even if conclusion is that GC basis is still
              appropriate</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;">
            <span>EPS (basic and diluted)</span><span
              ><span class="badge bp">SoPL</span></span
            ><span
              >On face or in notes; mandatory for listed entities (IAS 33)</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S19 – RELATED STANDARDS ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s19">
      <span class="num">19</span><h2>
        Related Standards – Cross-Reference Map
      </h2><span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>Standard</span><span>Nature of connection to IAS 1</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IAS 7</span><span
              >Statement of cash flows – IAS 1 requires it as part of a complete
              set; IAS 7 provides all the detailed rules for structure;
              direct/indirect method; classification of interest, dividends,
              taxes</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IAS 8</span><span
              >Accounting policies; changes in estimates; errors – directly
              triggers IAS 1's comparative restatement requirements and the
              third SoFP when a material retrospective change is made</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IAS 10</span><span
              >Events after the reporting period – determines whether
              post-year-end events (e.g. covenant waivers; dividend
              declarations) affect the current/non-current classification
              decisions made under IAS 1 at the reporting date</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IAS 12</span><span
              >Income taxes – deferred tax is always non-current under IAS 1;
              IAS 12 governs measurement; the tax reconciliation note required
              under IAS 12 complements IAS 1's disclosure framework</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IAS 33</span><span
              >Earnings per share – IAS 1 requires EPS to be presented for
              entities with publicly traded ordinary shares; IAS 33 provides
              detailed EPS calculation rules</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IAS 34</span><span
              >Interim financial reporting – sets the reduced content
              requirements for condensed interim statements, distinct from IAS
              1's full annual requirements</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IFRS 5</span><span
              >Non-current assets held for sale and discontinued operations –
              determines the separate presentation line items on the SoFP and
              SoPL face that IAS 1 prescribes as minimum line items</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IFRS 12</span><span
              >Disclosure of interests in other entities – the extensive
              disclosure requirements for subsidiaries, associates, JVs, and
              structured entities that supplement what IAS 1 captures in the
              primary statements</span
            >
          </div>
          <div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.7fr 2.5fr;">
            <span>IFRS 13</span><span
              >Fair value measurement – Level 1/2/3 hierarchy disclosures appear
              in the notes to the SoFP; the SoFP face shows carrying values but
              the notes (required by IFRS 13) explain FV measurement methodology</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ═══ S20 – GLOSSARY ═══ -->
    <div class="section-header" id="s20">
      <span class="num">20</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span
        class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="three-col">
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Fair presentation</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            The faithful representation of the effects of transactions, events
            and conditions in accordance with the definitions and recognition
            criteria set out in the Conceptual Framework. Achieved through
            compliance with IFRS; in extremely rare cases, departure from a
            specific IFRS requirement is permitted if compliance would be so
            misleading that it would conflict with the Framework's objective.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">
            Reclassification adjustments (recycling)
          </div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Amounts previously recognised in OCI that are reclassified to profit
            or loss in the current period – e.g. cumulative FX translation
            differences recycled on disposal of a foreign operation. IAS 1
            requires these to be separately identified in OCI in the period of
            recycling.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Operating cycle</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            The time between the acquisition of assets for processing and their
            realisation in cash or cash equivalents. When it is not clearly
            identifiable, IAS 1 assumes it to be twelve months. Inventory and
            receivables are current even when the cycle exceeds twelve months
            (e.g. distilleries; construction).
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Going concern</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            The assumption that an entity will continue in operation for the
            foreseeable future – it has neither the intention nor the need to
            liquidate or curtail the scale of its operations. When material
            uncertainties exist, they are disclosed. When the going concern
            basis is not used, IAS 1 requires disclosure of the alternative
            basis.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Total comprehensive income</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            The change in equity during a period resulting from transactions and
            other events, other than those changes resulting from transactions
            with owners in their capacity as owners. It comprises profit or loss
            plus other comprehensive income.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Non-controlling interests (NCI)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            The equity in a subsidiary not attributable, directly or indirectly,
            to a parent. Presented within equity in the consolidated SoFP –
            separately from the equity of the owners of the parent. Never
            classified between liabilities and equity under IFRS.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card cn">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">True and fair override</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            In the extremely rare circumstance where compliance with a specific
            IFRS requirement would be so misleading that it conflicts with the
            objective of financial statements, an entity may depart from that
            requirement. The departure, the reason, and the financial effect
            must all be disclosed. In practice, virtually never used.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">
            Material accounting policy information
          </div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Following the 2023 IAS 1 amendment: accounting policy information is
            material if it is expected to significantly affect amounts or
            disclosures. Entities should omit boilerplate policy descriptions
            that repeat IFRS wording without adding entity-specific insight –
            these do not meet the materiality threshold.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;">
          <div class="glossary-term">Estimation uncertainty (12-month)</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">
            Key assumptions about the future and other major sources of
            estimation uncertainty that have a significant risk of resulting in
            a material adjustment to the carrying amounts of assets or
            liabilities within the NEXT financial year. The "next financial
            year" time horizon is specific to this disclosure and distinguishes
            it from the judgements disclosure.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legend">
      <div class="ltitle">Statement abbreviations</div>
      <div class="lrow">
        <span class="badge bs">SoFP</span> Statement of financial position &nbsp;
        <span class="badge bp">SoPL</span> Statement of profit or loss &nbsp;
        <span class="badge bo">OCI</span> Other comprehensive income &nbsp;
        <span class="badge be">SoCE</span> Statement of changes in equity &nbsp;
        <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of cash flows &nbsp;
        <span class="badge bp">Notes</span> Notes to financial statements
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.IAS1} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

